=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nFrom the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+3z=7\\,⇒\\,x=7-3z\n$$\n\nand from the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\ny+2z=-3\\,⇒\\,y=-3-2z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3z \\\\ y=-3-2z \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7-3z \\\\ -3-2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399450 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399451 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399450 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399452 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399450 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399453 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399450 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399454 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399450 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399455 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399450 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399450 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399450 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399453 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399450 1080 #uuid "84f00b54-07f8-565a-95ff-d33549fee4dc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399451 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-3-3z \\\\ 7-2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399451 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399451 1084 #uuid "547016f8-709b-55ae-9ed1-84a5249a6fe5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399452 1081 "No solution" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399452 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399452 1084 #uuid "ad3871c3-7636-59b3-aaf5-402cb593106f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}7-3z \\\\ -3-2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1084 #uuid "92e86a7a-e842-58e1-a2ac-d05c185871b8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399454 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-7+3z \\\\ -3+2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399454 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399454 1084 #uuid "f8c294cf-9ff4-580b-9460-402477d8c46d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399455 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}7+3z \\\\ 3-2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399455 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399455 1084 #uuid "a20d4184-e472-531e-8a16-81dbaf3b46d3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399456 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399457 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399456 1069 "q-37853" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399456 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399456 1071 "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix $B$ has eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=4.$\nFind a diagonal matrix $D$ and an invertible matrix $P$ such that $D={P}^{-1}BP.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399456 1072 #uuid "197a265b-1aed-5f18-a576-60c74ff63df1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399456 1074 "We apply the diagonalization algorithm.\n\n**Step 1.**  Notice that we are already given the eigenvalues of the matrix: \n\n$\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{3}=4.$ \n\n**Step 2.** Now, we need to find an eigenvector basis of $A.$ Applying our usual method, we get the following.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-2I & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(B-2I)x=0$ gives us the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-(-2)I & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(B-(-2)I)x=0$ gives us the eigenvector ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{3}=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-4I & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(B-4I)x=0$ gives us the eigenvector ${v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 3.** We construct the diagonal matrix $D$ and the invertible matrix $P$ in the usual way, and this gives us the following:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399457 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399458 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399457 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399459 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399457 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399460 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399457 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399461 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399457 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399462 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399457 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399457 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399457 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399461 13194139533478 17592186045585 tru