7b1396-bf2f-5c6f-b4f9-47e505860659" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399476 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **velocity** $v$ of a merry-go-round **decreases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to the **velocity** at the moment.* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *velocity* of a merry-go-round \nvaries. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *velocity.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}∝v.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the velocity *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-kv.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399477 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399478 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399477 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399479 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399477 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399480 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399477 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399481 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399477 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399482 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399477 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399477 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399477 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399481 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399477 1080 #uuid "f9fafd73-05a6-5b8e-a964-c84cb300f7c1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399478 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=kt,\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399478 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399478 1084 #uuid "eb835d8b-6004-5f56-8811-1d5eadb295f5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399479 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=k{v}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399479 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399479 1084 #uuid "c85f9d07-a096-5a2e-95b7-531abb407759" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399480 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=kv,\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399480 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399480 1084 #uuid "19d3d09e-de67-502d-be1a-9e7be0611373" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399481 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-kv,\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399481 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399481 1084 #uuid "4d84ed1b-bffc-586f-8cf5-f8c7533c629e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399482 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-kt,\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399482 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399482 1084 #uuid "30dff20a-3979-523b-8f46-4a36c16bd1d3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399483 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399484 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399483 1069 "q-38108" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399483 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399483 1071 "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x+4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{2}+0x+16} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}+4x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4x-16}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,32\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399483 1072 #uuid "97a67cfa-cbb4-5ac8-9bbc-80fac24ef619" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399483 1074 "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+0x+16\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x-4 \\\\  & x+4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{2}+0x+16} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}+4x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,4x+16 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4x-16}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $x-4\\,$ and $\\,-4x+16.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399484 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399484 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399484 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399484 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399488 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399484 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399489 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399484 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399484 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399484 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399489 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399484 1080 #uuid "a2fc1b70-e6a0-5c8d-8800-110e15bde5bd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399485 1081 "$x-4\\,$ and $\\,-4x-16$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399485 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399485 1084 #uuid "43f269f8-0d49-548c-bc92-cc443a1f70f8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399486 1081 "$x+4\\,$ and $\\,4x-16$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399486 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399486 1084 #uuid "e9cd48ee-6c56-5ec9-b99c-7d68bdc0d094" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399487 1081 "$x-1\\,$ and $\\,-x+4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399487 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399487 1084 #uuid "0fe50aaf-85a4-5955-992f-838535becb8f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399488 1081 "$x+4\\,$ and $\\,4x+16$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399488 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399488 1084 #uuid "e5cff0b8-91ba-52ea-b5c7-0e5e4290afc6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399489 1081 "$x-4\\,$ and $\\,-4x+16$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399489 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399489 1084 #uuid "14b23255-8489-5a30-8112-1c64ab205295" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399490 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399491 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399490 1069 "q-38187" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399490 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399490 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $N$ given below?\n\nI. $N$ is **not** a singular matrix\nII. $N$ is a singular matrix\nIII. $det(N)=-1$\n\n$$\nN=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} & 3 & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & 4 & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & 5 & -\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399490 1072 #uuid "a5eb8a6b-37c6-54e6-b340-18101dbf3f8f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399490 1074 "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(N) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} & 3 & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & 4 & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & 5 & -\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}|\\begin{aligned}4 & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 5 & -\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & -\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}|+(-\\frac{1}{7})|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} & 4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}(-\\frac{4}{7}+\\frac{5}{7})-3(-\\frac{1}{49}+\\frac{1}{49})-\\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{5}{7}-\\frac{4}{7}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}-3\\cdot 0-\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{49}-\\frac{1}{49} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(N)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399491 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399492 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399491 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399491 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399494 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399491 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399495 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399491 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399496 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399491 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399491 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399491 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399496 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399491 1080 #uuid "22d26b64-8f4f-5847-bc42-645a93a0286d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399492 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399492 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399492 1084 #uuid "c0e0a56b-dd12-5f9a-a54c-f687e7197f5f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399493 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399493 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399493 1084 #uuid "c948f61c-0763-5a74-b23e-25debfd86016" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399494 1081 "III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399494 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399494 1084 #uuid "ea7451af-09f5-51f1-a1a1-522af10914c5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1084 #uuid "957a2ea8-95c2-5ef9-84c2-69527df0f48d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1081 "II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1084 #uuid "b1b56d91-8a6f-561f-b452-5b48fa80a33b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399497 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399498 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399497 1069 "q-38245" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399497 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399497 1071 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}+{v}^{2} \\\\ {u}^{2}-{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399497 1072 #uuid "48feab89-768b-5b8e-8c0a-02f86fdff070" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399497 1074 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={u}^{2}+{v}^{2}$ and $y(u,v)={u}^{2}-{v}^{2}.$ \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =2v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2u & 2v \\\\ 2u & -2v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2u\\cdot (-2v)-2v\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =-4uv-4uv \\\\  & =-8uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ -8uv & =0 \\\\ uv & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $uv=0$ defines the pair of intersecting lines $u=0$ and $v=0$ in the $uv$-plane. Notice that these lines correspond to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399498 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399498 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399498 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399501 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399498 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399502 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399498 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399503 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399498 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399498 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399498 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399501 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399498 1080 #uuid "f05d1ca1-306f-5d0c-970a-e108a73f246e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399499 1081 "The critical points lie on the lines $u+v=1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399499 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399499 1084 #uuid "9d467be4-da9c-5949-964e-fc1ece22124b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399500 1081 "The critical points lie on the line $u-v=1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399500 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399500 1084 #uuid "99d8765a-e6b9-5b6f-b95c-7ee236d3b208" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399501 1081 "The critical points lie on the lines $u=0$ and $v=0.$" 13194139533478 175