mon factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)(x+1)(x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the three solutions $x=-3,$ $x=-1$ and $x=1.$ Therefore, the equations of the vertical asymptotes are  $x=-3,\\,$ $x=-1$ and $x=1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399570 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399571 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399570 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399572 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399570 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399573 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399570 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399574 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399570 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399575 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399570 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399570 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399570 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399573 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399570 1080 #uuid "aba4d313-1d11-58c4-bb5b-3d3a12220a0e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399571 1081 "x=-1,\\,x=1,\\,x=3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399571 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399571 1084 #uuid "ce1c8713-2cf3-5d3e-be72-a3135dfaed78" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399572 1081 "x=-3,\\,x=1,\\,x=3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399572 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399572 1084 #uuid "fd5c07fd-aef8-50a6-bb7a-0214e75d1fbe" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399573 1081 "x=-3,\\,x=-1,\\,x=1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399573 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399573 1084 #uuid "b9d397dd-0706-56c3-a545-4f1e11b5d1fb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399574 1081 "x=-1,\\,x=1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399574 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399574 1084 #uuid "7d3acbb2-152b-5386-a5b3-d4d5f9778946" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399575 1081 "x=-1,\\,x=-\\frac{1}{3},\\,x=1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399575 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399575 1084 #uuid "466aa8d5-5559-5bc5-8a5d-ddd22b7bb453" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399576 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399577 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399576 1069 "q-39936" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399576 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399576 1071 "Determine the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{{x}^{4}-1}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399576 1072 #uuid "10e486fb-a153-567a-b122-83eab72817c1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399576 1074 "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{{x}^{4}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{({x}^{2}-1)({x}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-1)(x+1)}{(x-1)(x+1)({x}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x-1)(x+1)}}{\\cancel{(x-1)(x+1)}({x}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+1=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions. Therefore, $f(x)$ has no vertical asymptotes." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399577 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399578 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399577 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399579 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399577 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399580 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399577 1075