 2x-y \\\\ -5x+3y\\end{aligned}]$ and the vectors \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Which of the given vectors belong to $\\text{Ker}(T)?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399590 1072 #uuid "4bfe7ea3-d20b-5a92-b7ac-e6c2ec81d721" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399590 1074 "A vector $u$ belongs to the kernel of a linear transformation $T$ if $T(u)=0.$ \n\nTherefore, we need to compute $T({v}_{i})$ for each ${v}_{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({v}_{1}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{3}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\,T({v}_{i})\\ne 0$ for any $i$'s, we conclude that none of them belongs to the kernel of $\\,T.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399591 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399592 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399591 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399593 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399591 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399594 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399591 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399595 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399591 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399596 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399591 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399591 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399591 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399592 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399591 1080 #uuid "17572c2b-682c-5ae4-a962-e180a05850b2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399592 1081 "None of the given vectors belong to the kernel of $T$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399592 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399592 1084 #uuid "6db32447-a4ce-5dff-9487-a82e227e41f5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399593 1081 "${v}_{3}$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399593 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399593 1084 #uuid "8275882b-84f3-5627-93d4-2c259ae73a36" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399594 1081 "${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399594 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399594 1084 #uuid "814b7b1e-69ce-596a-8267-686227a9ea9c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399595 1081 "${v}_{1}$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399595 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399595 1084 #uuid "4a769e20-30bc-5034-8119-ec017476bd69" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399596 1081 "${v}_{2}$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399596 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399596 1084 #uuid "cfbec318-84b4-5cc1-a7c5-50ee378933cf" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399597 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399598 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399597 1069 "q-40277" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399597 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399597 1071 "Which of the following geometric series converge?\n\nI. $4+3+\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{27}{16}+⋯$\nII. $16-2+\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{32}+⋯$\nIII. $-8+16-32+64-⋯$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399597 1072 #uuid "5d6af0ce-2d7e-5e7e-9759-710fbc03ce1c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399597 1074 "Let's look at each series in turn.\n\n- For the geometric series $4+3+\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{27}{16}+⋯$  the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $16-2+\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{32}+⋯$ the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{-2}{16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $-8+16-32+64-⋯$  the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{16}{-8} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$\n\nIn conclusion, only series I and II converge." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399598 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399599 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399598 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399600 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399598 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399601 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399598 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399602 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399598 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399603 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399598 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399598 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399598 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399602 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399598 1080 #uuid "6140ca09-668b-5dd3-b823-6e3fa39bae3f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399599 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399599 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399599 1084 #uuid "58761f09-07f7-57a6-ab8e-19cc89659cdf" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399600 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399600 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399600 1084 #uuid "349f551e-f45b-5529-8d98-1ce5d2275f83" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399601 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399601 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17