6045585 true] [17592186399611 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399616 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399611 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399611 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399611 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399615 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399611 1080 #uuid "688252c3-b275-5ce8-9367-21ceb7930d2d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399612 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399612 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399612 1084 #uuid "abe0c444-f503-5e10-b6b5-dc687711397e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399613 1081 "{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399613 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399613 1084 #uuid "ab53f1ff-4095-5465-ba5a-7b95ae3035ad" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399614 1081 "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399614 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399614 1084 #uuid "26a36b7b-8c82-5f61-9f46-17a23ffa4851" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399615 1081 "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399615 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399615 1084 #uuid "851f5ba7-f81e-5caa-b027-397d46c4a3e3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399616 1081 "{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399616 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399616 1084 #uuid "86a6fd7d-2914-5ff6-a175-96b59582d072" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399617 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399618 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399617 1069 "q-41741" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399617 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399617 1071 "A small business collected data on the number of hours of telephone usage and the total amount (in hundreds of dollars) of the company's weekly operating expenses. This data is shown below.   \n\n| Hours $(x)$ | **$2$** | **$2.4$** | **$2.8$** | **$3.2$** | **$3.6$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Expenses $(y)$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n\nFind the line of the form $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above. According to the model, what will be the company's weekly operating expenses if the telephone is used for a total of $4$ hours per week, assuming the trend continues?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that*\n\n$$\n({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{8}[\\begin{aligned}40.8 & -14 \\\\ -14 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{X}^{T}y=[\\begin{aligned}30 \\\\ 88\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n*where $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector.*" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399617 1072 #uuid "d0007be5-4b39-5b13-9d0c-f56e380ce0f1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399617 1074 "The coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2.4 \\\\ 1 & 2.8 \\\\ 1 & 3.2 \\\\ 1 & 3.6\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\overset{^}{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values of $({X}^{T}X)^{-1}$ and ${X}^{T}y$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{\\beta } & =({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}\\,y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[\\begin{aligned}40.8 & -14 \\\\ -14 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}30 \\\\ 88\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2.5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the line $y=-1+2.5x.$\n\nFinally, to predict the amount of the company's weekly operating expenses if the telephone is used for a total of $4$ hours, we substitute $x=4$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1+2.5(4) \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, according to the model, the company's weekly operating expenses will be $$900.$ \n\n**Note**: Since we're extrapolating ($x=4$ is not within the range of the original set of $x$-values), our result *may* be unreliable." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399618 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399619 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399618 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399620 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399618 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399621 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399618 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399622 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399618 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399623 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399618 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399618 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399618 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399622 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399618 1080 #uuid "ba3cb994-1bad-5429-8732-d77a5dada295" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399619 1081 "$$1\\,050$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399619 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [1759